# Implement optional audio and video transcription

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical domain evidence does not imply a working adapter. The finite
contract preserves explicit unavailable capabilities.

Normalize supported media to bounded temporary audio, invoke the admitted
WhisperX adapter, preserve word timing and confidence, and always clean up.

Current executable evidence now freezes a transport-neutral derived transcript
separate from original media and any particular transcription engine. It retains
original media kind/identity, unique job identity, and replaceable engine
identity inside one typed origin bundle. It also retains resolved word order,
optional word timing/confidence/speaker evidence, and
explicit unresolved fragments. Media decoding, bounded waveform conversion,
WhisperX invocation, job progress/cancellation, temporary storage, and cleanup
remain open adapter/lifecycle work.

Terminal media-job cleanup state is now executable independently of filesystem
implementation. Success, cancellation, and handled failure all remain unsettled
while an owned waveform intermediate is pending cleanup; cleanup failure becomes
an explicit retry-required state, and an intermediate owned by another job
rejects. An exhaustive 18-state oracle crosses all three terminal outcomes with
no intermediate, pending cleanup, or retry-required cleanup and matching versus
foreign ownership; outcome never weakens cleanup or ownership requirements.
Temporary path selection, actual deletion, retry scheduling/limits, process
interruption recovery, decoder/engine invocation, and persistence remain open
application/adapter work.

A process-local media-job application service now owns opaque job and waveform
identities around that terminal rule. One active job can register at most one
waveform intermediate, terminal outcome cannot be rewritten, cleanup failure
remains retry-required, and recorded cleanup success is the only transition to
Settled after an intermediate existed; late cleanup success or failure for that
retired intermediate rejects without recreating cleanup work. A 12-path state
machine oracle crosses all three terminal outcomes with no waveform, pending
cleanup, failed cleanup, and failed-then-successful cleanup so outcome cannot
change session cleanup transitions.

Dropping the service leaves a fresh owner with no prior job authority. The
service still chooses no path, creates or deletes no file, invokes no decoder or
engine, and schedules no retry.

## Finite optional local media intake and cleanup contract

**Inputs:** one user-authorized local WAV audio clip of at most 30 seconds
or one MP4 video clip at most 30 seconds/16 MiB, source identity, decoder
capabilities and optional locally installed WhisperX. **Outputs:** an
immutable source-linked word-timed transcript with speaker/confidence
observations or `UnavailableAdapter`, plus a terminal cleanup receipt.
No media gets uploaded, transcribed or decoded by a theoretical contract.

**Audio example:** WAV `a1` contains a 12-second spoken explanation. Decode
at declared 16 kHz mono PCM into a private job-scoped temporary waveform;
WhisperX, only if installed and explicitly admitted, returns timed words
with start/end seconds, speaker if known, reported confidence and unresolved
spans. An MP4 `v1` of 18 seconds/8 MiB uses the same bounded temporary audio
normalization, preserving original video source ID and timestamp offset.
All results remain candidate evidence, never an accepted notebook edit.

**Lifecycle:** use one opaque job ID and at most one waveform intermediate.
After success, failure or cancellation, request cleanup; only recorded
success settles a job after intermediate creation. If cleanup fails, retain
`CleanupRequired` and an owned retry obligation; never report safe cleanup
on attempted deletion alone. A process restart with no previous job authority
must not claim it knows which old files were removed.

**Refusal example:** a 31-second recording, unsupported codec, missing
WhisperX, denied local media permission, ambiguous timestamp or decode
failure returns exact non-transcript evidence. Stale cleanup callbacks
cannot reopen a settled job; silence never turns unknown speech into text.

**Assumptions and limits:** transport-neutral transcript evidence, terminal
cleanup states and a process-local job lifecycle service exist, but no media
path, decoder, WhisperX adapter, actual temporary-file deletion, retry
scheduler or source persistence is wired. This is a design-only intake.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for job/cleanup state primitives; theoretical for
  actual media decoding and transcription, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** one short WAV and one short MP4 case, duration/byte bounds,
  word timing/confidence and cleanup failure/refusal states.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** decoder, WhisperX execution,
  secure temporary file lifecycle or real transcript output.
